      "id": "write-instrument",
      "pattern": "[Verb] + بِالـ[Instrument]",
      "exampleArabic": "أكتب بالقلم",
      "exampleTransliteration": "aktubu bi-l-qalami",
      "exampleEnglish": "I write with the pen.",
      "grammarNote": "كتب conjugates fully regularly, like ذهب/شرب/عمل. بِ ('with/by', showing the tool used to do something) is a prefix like وَ and الـ — it attaches directly, no space: بِالْقَلَمِ, not بِ الْقَلَمِ. كِتَاب ('book', level 3) and كَتَبَ/يَكْتُبُ ('wrote'/'writes') share the same root ك-ت-ب — Arabic vocabulary is built from three-letter roots this way, so recognizing a root often helps you guess a related word's meaning.",
      "audio": { "id": "phrase_aktubu_bialqalam", "text": "أكتب بالقلم" },
      "introducedInLevel": 34
    }
